<p>In my unprofessional opinion, it pretty accurately conveys the growing apprehension of being lost. Only one thing really bugged me<span style="text-decoration: line-through;">in the last Exploration Log, I noticed that the D-Class referred to each other based on their designation numbers. Unless, for whatever reason, they were forbidden from the use of names, most people</span> especially in isolation&#8212; would likely use first names.</p>
<p>Grisly as it is, I like the alt-history horror of the ship discovery. It made me go on a wild jaunt of speculation, and I love it when an SCP article does that.</p>

